    {
      "id": "location-7",
      "lat": 43.063849950314705,
      "lng": -76.16946527202623,
      "zoom": 15.34498283956006,
      "html": "<p>Once an industrial scrapyard and oil tank field at the southern tip of Onondaga Lake, the area surrounding Destiny USA and the Inner Harbor underwent a dramatic shift from toxic waste site to commercial centerpiece. Opened in 1990 as Carousel Center, the venue expanded and rebranded in 2012 as Destiny USA—a massive indoor mall packed with retail and unique entertainment, including high-speed indoor go-karting. Next door, public cleanup efforts transformed the harbor basin itself—adding trails, an amphitheater, and modern housing to turn a neglected industrial waterfront into a thriving regional destination. In the near future, a public aquarium will be at the center of the Inner Harbor.</p>",
      "flyTransition": "smooth",
