    {
      "id": "location-6",
      "lat": 43.07748783113659,
      "lng": -76.19985128490691,
      "zoom": 10.120290906346105,
      "html": "<p>For over a century, Onondaga Lake suffered severe pollution from industrial waste, including massive mercury deposits from chemical manufacturing and untreated municipal sewage. In response to its 1994 Superfund listing, a major remediation effort upgraded wastewater treatment, dredged millions of cubic yards of toxic sediment, and capped the lakebed. </p><p><br></p><p>While water quality and local wildlife have made a remarkable recovery, ongoing monitoring and debates remain over whether capping offers enough long-term protection.</p>",
      "flyTransition": "smooth",
      "overlays": {
        "geojson": {
          "type": "FeatureCollection",
          "features": []
        }
      },
      "baseMap": "esri-satellite"
    },
    {
      "id": "location-8",
      "lat": 42.840231660370776,
      "lng": -76.9827260915215,
      "zoom": 8.77674738196139,
      "html": "<p>Easily accessible by car, the nearby Finger Lakes offer lots of outdoor activities, shopping and wine tasting for tourists. </p><p>Carved by ancient glaciers, the Finger Lakes region is defined by eleven long, narrow lakes surrounded by dramatic gorges, cascading waterfalls, and rolling hills. Visitors flock to the region to sample world-class Rieslings along scenic wine trails, hike through breathtaking state parks like Watkins Glen, and explore charming lakeside towns that blend rich American history with vibrant local culture.</p>",
      "flyTransition": "smooth",
      "overlays": {
        "geojson": {
          "type": "FeatureCollection",
          "features": []
        }
      },
      "baseMap": "esri-satellite"
    },
    {
      "id": "location-9",
      "lat": 43.767311480501576,
      "lng": -76.22574561901456,
      "zoom": 12.181256656972018,
      "html": "<p>At the eastern end of Lake Ontario, there's a great public beach called Southwick Beach State Park. It's famous for its long, golden stretches of sand and ocean-like freshwater waves.</p><p>A favorite destination for swimmers, campers, and sunbathers, the park borders the protected Lake Ontario Dune Center, offering scenic boardwalk trails that wind through rare coastal sand dunes and wetlands. Whether you're pitching a tent steps from the beach, paddling along the shoreline, or watching a sunset over the lake, Southwick delivers a quintessential East Coast beach experience right in Upstate New York.</p>",
      "flyTransition": "smooth",
      "overlays": {
        "geojson": {
          "type": "FeatureCollection",
          "features": []
        }
      },
      "baseMap": "esri-satellite"
    },
    {
      "id": "location-10",
      "lat": 47.69065679520004,
      "lng": -81.48345799513731,
      "zoom": 4.271410403793278,
      "html": "<p>If you're itching to get out of Syracuse, you have plenty of other options. Syracuse serves as an ideal launchpad for road trips across the Northeast and eastern Canada. Within a 4- to 5-hour drive, you can reach several major metropolitan hubs:</p><ul><li><strong>New York City (~4 hrs):</strong> Head south down I-81 and I-80 for world-class dining, Broadway, and iconic urban sights.</li><li><strong>Toronto (~4.5 hrs):</strong> Drive west past Niagara Falls to explore Canada’s largest skyline, diverse neighborhoods, and vibrant waterfront.</li><li><strong>Montreal (~4.5 hrs):</strong> Head straight north past the Thousand Islands to experience Old World European charm, festival life, and French-Canadian cuisine. </li></ul><p><br></p>",
      "flyTransition": "smooth",
